 distance added to the GeometryInstance3D’s bounding box (","type":"text"},{"code":"AABB","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") to increase its cull box.","type":"text"}]},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/GeometryInstance3D/transparency":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/GeometryInstance3D\/transparency","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The transparency applied to the whole geometry (as a multiplier of the materials’ existing transparency). "},{"code":"0.0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is fully opaque, while "},{"code":"1.0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is fully transparent. Values greater than "},{"code":"0.0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (exclusive) will force the geometry’s materials to go through the transparent pipeline, which is slower to render and can exhibit rendering issues due to incorrect transparency sorting. However, unlike using a transparent material, setting "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/GeometryInstance3D\/transparency","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" to a value greater than "},{"code":"0.0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (exclusive) will "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"not","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" disable shadow rendering."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"transparency","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"title":"transparency","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/geometryinstance3d\/transparency","kind":"symbol"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/GeometryInstance3D/visibilityRangeBegin":{"title":"visibilityRangeBegin","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Starting distance from which the GeometryInstance3D will be visible, taking "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGo